<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-11787] Thin client: Protocol version conflict in master</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-11787</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Two independent tickets (&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-11043&quot; title=&quot;CPP Thin: Improve Best Effort Affinity for C++ thin client&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-11043&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-11043&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9113&quot; title=&quot;Allocate memory for a data region when first cache assigned to this region is created&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-9113&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-9113&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) introduced two different thin protocol versions - one for Affinity Awareness and another is for the Lazy Memory Allocation. These two different protocol versions were given the same value - 1.3.0. It is proposed to change one of versions to 1.4.0.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
